Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:25:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] seam: pin SearchResultRows row de-duplication

Promoting SearchResultRows to IControlCore moved the consecutive-
duplicate filtering out of TermControl and behind the interface, because
til::point_span is not projectable. That relocated real observable
behaviour with no test covering it.

TestSearchResultRowsAreDistinct pins the resulting contract: one entry
per matching row, ascending, regardless of how many times the term
occurs on that row. Three matches across two rows yield two entries.

Mutation-tested: removing the dedup guard fails with Values (2, 3).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ee27Fih3vSPYsqrUBpUoc
---
 .../UnitTests_Control/ControlCoreTests.cpp    | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/ControlCoreTests.cpp b/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/ControlCoreTests.cpp
index da0ffa365..4b2f72576 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/ControlCoreTests.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/ControlCoreTests.cpp
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@ namespace ControlUnitTests
 
         TEST_METHOD(TestIsBufferRowInViewport);
         TEST_METHOD(TestIsBufferRowInViewportAltBuffer);
+        TEST_METHOD(TestSearchResultRowsAreDistinct);
 
         TEST_CLASS_SETUP(ModuleSetup)
